			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Tracing module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Tracing/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `now` -> `Now`, `correlation_id` -> `CorrelationId`) in method implementations.\n- Renaming utility function calls to match the PascalCase convention (e.g., `generate_request_id()` -> `GenerateRequestId()`, `current_timestamp()` -> `CurrentTimestamp()`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `:u64` instead of `: u64`, `:String` instead of `: String`).\n- Reorganizing imports for logical grouping and collapsing complex `std::panic::catch_unwind` chains for conciseness.\n- Updating documentation comments to use relative project paths (e.g., `vs/base/common/errors`) instead of absolute file system paths.\n\nThis ensures the `Tracing` module, responsible for distributed tracing, span collection, and context propagation within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
