			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Security module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Security/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting struct fields within `SecureBytes` and `SecurityEvent` from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `data` -> `Data`, `event_type` -> `EventType`).\n- Renaming function parameters and local variables in method implementations to `PascalCase` (e.g., `s` -> `S`, `other` -> `Other`).\n- Updating calls to utility functions to match the new naming convention (e.g., `current_timestamp()` -> `CurrentTimestamp()`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `:Vec<u8>` instead of `: Vec<u8>`).\n- Cleaning up trailing whitespace in documentation comments.\n\nThis ensures the `Security` module, responsible for encryption, secure storage, and audit logging within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
