			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Resilience module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Resilience/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting function parameters and local variables throughout the module from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `service` -> `Service`, `attempt` -> `Attempt`, `config` -> `Config`).\n- Renaming public methods to match the PascalCase naming convention (e.g., `GetState`, `ValidateConfig`, `GetStatistics`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `:u64` instead of `: u64`) and reorganizing imports for logical grouping.\n- Updating documentation comments to use relative project paths (e.g., `vs/base/common/errors`) instead of absolute file system paths.\n- Refactoring `BulkheadExecutor::Execute` to streamline permit acquisition and queue management logic.\n\nThis ensures the `Resilience` module, responsible for fault tolerance, circuit breaking, and retry policies within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
