			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Plugins module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and variable naming normalization to the `Source/Plugins/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables within `PluginManager` and `PluginLoader` methods from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `discovered` -> `Discovered`, `results` -> `Results`).\n- Renaming private helper methods to match the PascalCase convention (e.g., `check_api_version_compatibility` -> `CheckApiVersionCompatibility`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `directory: &str` -> `directory:&str`) in function signatures and struct definitions.\n- Collapsing `use` imports into single-line blocks and condensing simple `Default` and `PluginHooks` implementations for conciseness.\n- Updating documentation comments to reference relative project paths (e.g., `vs/platform/extensions/common/`) instead of absolute file system paths.\n\nThis ensures the `Plugins` module, responsible for the Air daemon's extensibility, sandboxing, and inter-plugin communication, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
