			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Metrics module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Metrics/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting function parameters and local variables throughout the module from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `latency_seconds` -> `LatencySeconds`, `current` -> `Current`).\n- Renaming struct fields within helper types (`MetricGuard`, `AggregationValidator`, `MetricsData`) to PascalCase for consistency.\n- Updating private helper functions to match the PascalCase naming convention (e.g., `min_max_update` -> `MinMaxUpdate`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `:u64` instead of `: u64`) and reorganizing imports for logical grouping.\n- Adjusting documentation comments to use relative project paths instead of absolute file system paths.\n\nThis ensures the `Metrics` module, responsible for Prometheus-compatible telemetry collection and performance monitoring within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
